From 1f5f9af5622caca41f9b2e483e550c504f99dac9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:07:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: revert PCIe iommu-map to 1-cell
 format
X-Original-Commit: ce3e266f9e048c16c884ec7cd3422ab1ff2f890d
X-Original-Committer: Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
X-Original-Committer-Date: 2026-10-10T08:10:19-05:00

The upstream stable commit 36fb7eea7 changed the PCIe iommu-map from
1-cell to 2-cell format (adding SID mask) to silence an OF core
warning.  On the OnePlus Pad 4 (iceland), this breaks WiFi entirely:
the WCN7860 PCIe device loses its SMMU stream mapping, MHI cannot
initialize ('Device link is not accessible'), and no WiFi interface
appears.  Bluetooth (UART) is unaffected.

Revert the kaanapali DTS change to the 1-cell format that works on
this board.  The proper fix needs investigation of why the 2-cell
SID mask 0x0 fails here (possibly apps_smmu configuration).

Verified: WiFi fully functional with only this revert on v7.2.9.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index 61c1099842f0ea6886cad32f98c631554009d9f3..a2148fcac7792f5f8a77cca93bc2e1dd2642bd92 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -2481,8 +2481,8 @@ &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>,
 
 			operating-points-v2 = <&pcie0_opp_table>;
 
-			iommu-map = <0 &apps_smmu 0x1400 0x0 0x1>,
-				    <0x100 &apps_smmu 0x1401 0x0 0x1>;
+			iommu-map = <0 &apps_smmu 0x1400 0x1>,
+				    <0x100 &apps_smmu 0x1401 0x1>;
 
 			interrupt-map = <0 0 0 1 &intc 0 0 GIC_SPI 149 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 					<0 0 0 2 &intc 0 0 GIC_SPI 150 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
